    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1035">

                <pb facs="1082" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg796"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860c.01/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-11-05T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 5, 1916, 2 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 6, 1.30 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4562. In a manifest published to-day the Emperors of Germany and of
                    Austria-Hungary proclaim Poland as an independent state with hereditary monarchy
                    and constitution. The exact boundaries of the Kingdom of Poland to be decided
                    later. Text of manifest will be cabled to-morrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
